WEBVTT

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:04.640
Night-operation requirements vary by jurisdiction, aircraft, purpose, location,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.240
and operating framework.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.515
Check current official aviation sources before flight.

00:00:08.515 --> 00:00:10.960
Do not rely on an old checklist, a social post,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.805
or software geofencing as a complete legal determination.

00:00:14.805 --> 00:00:18.580
Requirements may address pilot qualification, aircraft registration or identification,

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:23.040
anti-collision lighting, visual line of sight, airspace authorization, observers, records,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.400
and operations near people or vehicles.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.035
Local rules and property access may add separate obligations.

00:00:28.035 --> 00:00:33.080
Define the mission purpose, area, route, altitude strategy, required imagery, crew roles,

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.750
and duration.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.595
Confirm the site is authorized and that collection will not extend into unnecessary

00:00:37.595 --> 00:00:39.470
private areas or sensitive locations.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.720
Review airspace, temporary restrictions, airports, emergency activity, obstacles, terrain,

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.180
weather, temperature, lighting, and nearby operations.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.890
Visit or review the site in daylight when appropriate so hidden wires, branches,

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.840
structures, and landing hazards are known before darkness.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.840
Set go or no-go and abort criteria.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.240
These may include minimum visibility, acceptable wind, battery condition,

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.995
lighting function, navigation confidence, signal quality, crew readiness,

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:04.360
and a clear recovery area.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.930
Use limits appropriate to official requirements and manufacturer guidance.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.650
Document the sources checked, approvals, aircraft, crew, weather, site findings,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.135
risk controls, return settings, emergency options, and decision.

00:01:15.135 --> 00:01:19.320
When authority or conditions are unclear, delay the flight and obtain qualified guidance.
